From: mscharged-port native source preparation
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve original EFB while resizing native window output
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

Keep source EFB/depth/cache storage across physical surface-only resize.
Native VIConfigure exposes its requested GX descriptor immediately, as the
original SDK does, while physical VI register latching remains delayed.
Retire genuine pending source FIFO/GPU work before a real EFB allocation
change; emit no synthetic GX completion, VI retrace or source frame.
Existing SC display aspect and original VI rectangle/positioning remain
unchanged. Game source, camera, projection and layout are not patched.

